-- title:
--   Gauge majorisation passes to spans of right translates
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, with ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_F$, and write $G = \mathrm{GL}_3$ of the adele ring of $\mathcal{O}_F$ in $F$. Let $W : G \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfy `IsGaugeMajorised3`, that is: there are $t \in \mathbb{N}$, a finite set $T$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_F$ and a real $B$ such that for every $N \in \mathbb{N}$ there is a constant $C$ with, for all $g \in G$, both $W g = 0$ whenever $g$ fails `InRootLevel` for $T$ and $B$ (i.e. whenever some $v \notin T$ has $\mathrm{finRoot}_1(v,g) > 1$ or $\mathrm{finRoot}_2(v,g) > 1$, or some $v \in T$ has one of these roots exceeding $B$), and $\|W g\| \le C / \bigl(\mathrm{rootSizeProd}(g)^t (1 + \mathrm{archRootSum}(g))^N\bigr)$ whenever $g$ does satisfy `InRootLevel` for $T$ and $B$. Let $W'$ lie in `gl3CyclicSubspace W`, the $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of functions $G \to \mathbb{C}$ spanned by the right translates $h \mapsto W(h g)$ for $g \in G$. Then $W'$ again satisfies `IsGaugeMajorised3`, for some possibly different data $t$, $T$, $B$ and constants.
--
--   This is the stability of the mirabolic gauge majorant — the support and moderate-growth bound governing Whittaker functions on $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over the adeles — under passage from a single function to the span of its right translates. It is used to transfer the majorisation to members of the cyclic module generated by a Whittaker function, in the construction of cubic induction data and in the statements combining gauge majorisation with moment and half-plane properties.
